language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Golomb ruler: a set of marks, starting at 0, with all pairwise differences distinct, and minimum length.
given size : int(2..)
find marks : matrix indexed by [int(1..size)] of int(0..size*size)
$ the length of the ruler is the position of its last mark
find length : int(0..size*size)

branching on [marks]
minimising length
such that
$ the first mark is at position 0
marks[1] = 0,
$ the marks are in increasing order, so the ruler's positions are distinct and sorted
forAll i : int(1..size-1) . (marks[i] < marks[i+1]),
$ all m(m-1)/2 differences between pairs of marks are distinct
allDiff([marks[j] - marks[i] | i : int(1..size), j : int(1..size), i < j]),
$ the length of the ruler is the position of its last mark
length = marks[size]
